# Candidate Fit Predictor — ML Zoomcamp 2026 Midterm Project

An end-to-end machine learning inference service and web application that predicts candidate hiring outcomes (`fit` / `no-fit`) from structured recruitment analytics data.

* **Live Web Application:** [career-oracle-ml.netlify.app](https://career-oracle-ml.netlify.app)
* **Dataset Source:** [`automated_recruitment_analytics.csv`](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zm412/machine-learning-zoomcamp/refs/heads/main/midterm/automated_recruitment_analytics.csv)

---

## 1. Problem Description
Manual resume screening and early-stage candidate triage are time-consuming and prone to inconsistent evaluation criteria. **Candidate Fit Predictor** addresses this by scoring candidate profiles based on historical recruitment outcomes, providing recruiters and hiring managers with an automated compatibility probability to prioritize qualified applicants.

* **Task Type:** Binary Classification (`0` = Rejected / No Fit, `1` = Hired / Fit)
* **Primary Evaluation Metric:** ROC-AUC (chosen due to class imbalance in hiring outcomes, ~89% negative vs. ~11% positive) alongside Precision, Recall, and Confusion Matrix analysis.

---

## 2. Dataset & Feature Processing
The model is trained on [`automated_recruitment_analytics.csv`](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zm412/machine-learning-zoomcamp/refs/heads/main/midterm/automated_recruitment_analytics.csv).

* **Input Features:** Eight observable candidate profile attributes covering experience, skills, and application metadata.
* **Missing Value Handling:** Missing numeric values are imputed using training-set medians stored in `feature_defaults.json`; missing categorical values are imputed as `'NA'`.
* **Encoding & Vectorization:** Categorical and numerical features are transformed using `DictVectorizer` prior to model training and inference.

---

## 3. Repository Structure
```text
midterm/
├── automated_recruitment_analytics.csv   # Training & validation dataset
├── notebook.ipynb                        # EDA, feature importance, cross-validation & model selection
├── train.py                              # Script to train the final model and export artifacts
├── predict.py                            # FastAPI inference service (/health and /predict)
├── smoke_test.py                         # Automated endpoint verification script
├── feature_defaults.json                 # Training medians for missing numeric feature imputation
├── model_metadata.json                   # Artifact checksums and model metadata
├── pyproject.toml & uv.lock              # Reproducible dependency lockfile managed by Astral uv
├── Dockerfile                            # Container specification with pinned base image digests
└── README.md                             # Project documentation
